---
layout: "home"
date: Last Modified
permalink: "/index.html"
localCSS: ["home"]
---

{% from "macros/section-bar.njk" import sectionBar %}
{% from "macros/gutter-list.njk" import entryRow, postRow %}
{% from "macros/work-list.njk" import workList %}

{#
    Four practices, one alignment line. Every section is a bar and a gutter
    list, and every title in every list starts at the same horizontal position
    — which is the whole device the page has, there being no images.

    WRITING and THINKING read their own collections newest-first, so
    publishing is what changes this page. Nothing here is hand-ordered.

    WORKING comes last and reads src/_data/roles.js. It is the one section
    whose rows link nowhere, because no role has a page: the history is short
    enough to be the section rather than an index of one, and the bar sends
    anyone who wants the long form to LinkedIn.
#}
{% set essays = collections.writing | reverse | head(6) %}
{% set thoughts = collections.thinking | reverse | head(4) %}

<section class="hero">
    <p class="hero__statement">Sean Voisen is a software design and engineering leader working on <strong>making computers better for human thinking &amp; creativity.</strong></p>
    {#
    <dl class="hero__sub">
        <div class="hero__sub-line">
            <dt class="hero__sub-label">By day</dt><dd class="hero__sub-text">Shipping code and leading teams.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__sub-line">
            <dt class="hero__sub-label">By night</dt><dd class="hero__sub-text">Plotter art and <a href="https://moonpointing.org">essays on philosophy</a>.</dd>
        </div>
    </dl>
    #}
</section>

<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Writing", "All essays", "/writing/") }}
    <ul class="gutter-grid">
    {%- for post in essays %}
    {{ postRow(post, post.date | monthYear) }}
    {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Thinking", "All posts", "/thinking/") }}
    <ul class="gutter-grid">
    {%- for post in thoughts %}
    {{ postRow(post, post.date | monthYear) }}
    {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
</section>

{# No right-hand link: there is no "all reading" page to point at, and the
   Directory is already in the header. #}
<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Reading") }}
    <ul class="gutter-grid">
        {{ entryRow("", "Bookshelf", "Books I've read, grouped by year.", "/bookshelf/") }}
        {{ entryRow("", "Philosophy for designers", "A reading list and a self-study journey.", "/philosophy-for-designers/") }}
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Working", "LinkedIn", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/svoisen/") }}
    {{ workList(roles) }}
</section>
